various sources of carbohydrates</article-title><source>J Sci Food Agric</source><year>1993</year><volume>63</volume><fpage>397</fpage><lpage>406</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0011"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henningsson</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bj&#x000f6;rck</surname><given-names>IM</given-names></name><name><surname>Nyman</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Combinations of indigestible carbohydrates affect short-chain fatty acid formation in the hindgut of rats</article-title><source>J Nutr</source><year>2002</year><volume>132</volume><fpage>3098</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12368401</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0012"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henningsson</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Nyman</surname><given-names>MEGL</given-names></name><name><surname>Bj&#x000f6;rck</surname><given-names>IM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influences of dietary adaptation and source of resistant starch on short-chain fatty acids in the hindgut of rats</article-title><source>Br J Nutr</source><year>2003</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>319</fpage><lpage>28</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12628027</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT0013"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nilsson</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Nyman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahrn&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sullivan</surname><given-names>EO</given-names></name><name><surname>Fitzgerald</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bifidobacterium